# ── SLBF environment variables ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to .env for local development. Production values are set in the host's
# environment, never in a file (SDR §14, §15).
#
# Anything marked REQUIRED is checked at start-up by src/lib/env.ts and the
# server refuses to boot without it.

# ── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED. Postgres, in every environment including local development. On a
# serverless host each instance opens its own pool, so this must be the host's
# *pooled* connection string, not the direct endpoint — the direct one runs the
# database out of connections as soon as traffic spreads over a few instances.
#
# Neon calls the pooled host `...-pooler.<region>.aws.neon.tech`; `sslmode=require`
# is not optional on any hosted provider.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host-pooler.region.aws.neon.tech/fbf?sslmode=require"

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED. Generate per environment with: openssl rand -base64 48
# TICKET_SECRET signs the HMAC in every QR e-ticket. Rotating it invalidates
# every ticket already issued, so rotate it between events, not during one.
#
# Sessions deliberately have no secret: the cookie carries an opaque random
# token and only its SHA-256 is stored, so there is nothing to sign and a
# leaked backup yields no usable cookies (src/lib/auth.ts).
TICKET_SECRET=""

# REQUIRED. Absolute public URL — used in emails, QR links and canonical tags.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# ── Payments (FR-07) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# "sandbox" simulates the full authorise → webhook → confirm cycle with no
# external calls. "live" requires every variable below — src/lib/env.ts fails
# the boot rather than let the site take registrations it cannot collect on.
PAYMENTS_MODE="sandbox"

ORANGE_MONEY_BASE_URL=""
ORANGE_MONEY_MERCHANT_ID=""
ORANGE_MONEY_API_KEY=""
ORANGE_MONEY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""

AFRIMONEY_BASE_URL=""
AFRIMONEY_MERCHANT_ID=""
AFRIMONEY_API_KEY=""
AFRIMONEY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""

# Card payments use the PSP's hosted page. No card data reaches this
# application and none is ever stored (NFR-06). There is no publishable key
# here because nothing PSP-related runs in the browser: the checkout session
# is created server-to-server and the delegate is redirected to it.
CARD_PSP_BASE_URL=""
CARD_PSP_SECRET_KEY=""
CARD_PSP_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""

# ── File uploads (§4.14) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL, and the admin panel adapts to its absence rather than breaking.
#
# With this set, the media library, the article and speaker forms and the page
# editor all offer a "choose a file" button beside their address field, and the
# file goes from the editor's browser straight to Vercel Blob. Without it those
# buttons are not rendered at all and staff paste an address instead — which is
# still how a film on YouTube or a document on a ministry's site gets onto the
# site either way.
#
# Vercel sets this automatically on a deployment once a Blob store is connected
# to the project (Storage → Create → Blob). For local development, copy the
# value from the store's settings; uploads made locally land in the same store
# as production, so prefer a separate store if that matters.
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=""

# ── Communications (FR-08) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Messages are written to the message_outbox table first and dispatched second.
# "log" records and logs them; "http" POSTs to the provider endpoint below.
MAIL_MODE="log"
MAIL_FROM="no-reply@fbf.sl"
MAIL_API_URL=""
MAIL_API_KEY=""

SMS_MODE="log"
SMS_SENDER_ID="FBF"
SMS_GATEWAY_URL=""
SMS_GATEWAY_KEY=""

# Where staff notifications go (new enquiries, offline payments to reconcile).
SECRETARIAT_EMAIL="secretariat@fbf.sl"
